# Maintainer: Yūrei Linux project
# Yūrei's own recipe (stage 3, the desktop; docs/INDEPENDENT.md). The source
# address and sum are the ones in independent/bootstrap/sources.lock;
# check-recipes.py keeps them the same.
pkgname=cmake
pkgver=3.31.7
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Build system generator (LLVM, SPIR-V tools and glslang build with it)"
arch=(x86_64)
url="https://cmake.org/"
license=(BSD-3-Clause)
depends=(glibc gcc-libs curl libarchive expat zlib bzip2 xz zstd openssl ncurses)
source=("https://github.com/Kitware/CMake/releases/download/v$pkgver/cmake-$pkgver.tar.gz")
sha256sums=('a6d2eb1ebeb99130dfe63ef5a340c3fdb11431cce3d7ca148524c125924cea68')

build() {
    cd cmake-$pkgver
    # Yūrei's own libraries where it has them; CMake's bundled copies of
    # the rest (jsoncpp, libuv, rhash)
    ./bootstrap --prefix=/usr --mandir=/share/man --docdir=/share/doc/cmake \
        --parallel="$(nproc)" --system-curl --system-expat --system-zlib \
        --system-bzip2 --system-liblzma --system-zstd --system-libarchive \
        -- -DCMAKE_USE_OPENSSL=ON -DBUILD_CursesDialog=OFF
    make
}

package() {
    cd cmake-$pkgver
    make DESTDIR="$pkgdir" install
}
